From 153ced2be069d82b11014027ddb5b1a2c4a3edd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:53:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(sync): widen the scripts in place, and start from a
 chain state

UpdateSubscriber::widen_handle() takes the last index to watch per
keychain, applied before the next event: the index derives the scripts
through it and the filters are checked against them from then on. That
covers addresses the wallet revealed since the node was built, and with
Requester::rescan_from the running node scans again for a wider window
without a new node and without downloading headers again.

BuilderExt::build_with_wallet_from() builds the node from a given chain
state, such as a snapshot of headers the caller already holds and
checked, instead of the policy's checkpoint.
